.\" Manpage for net.
.TH NET 1 "2026-08-25" "net 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
net \- list macOS network interfaces and their IPv4 addresses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B net
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B net
enumerates the network interfaces on a macOS system and prints, for each one,
its BSD interface name, the localized hardware port name, its IPv4 address,
its MAC address and its link status. In the long view it additionally reports
the maximum negotiated bandwidth and the adapter serial number.
.PP
Interface names and hardware port names are resolved through the
.B SystemConfiguration
framework, so they match the labels shown in System Settings. Link speed is
decoded from the interface media word, and serial numbers are read from the
IOKit registry.
.PP
By default only active interfaces are listed, and only the Hardware Port and
IPv4 Address columns are shown. Output is colorized only when standard output
is a terminal, so redirecting or piping the output yields clean plain text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show all interfaces, including inactive ones. Inactive rows are rendered in
dimmed colors.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-long
Long view: show every column, adding maximum bandwidth and serial number to
the default set.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-table
Render a bordered table using
.BR ncurses (3)
instead of plain text. The table is shown in a full-screen window; press any
key to exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
An unknown option was given, or the interface list could not be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the active interfaces:
.PP
.RS
.nf
net
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show every interface with all columns:
.PP
.RS
.nf
net \-al
.fi
.RE
.PP
Render the full table in ncurses:
.PP
.RS
.nf
net \-\-table \-\-long
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ifconfig (8),
.BR networksetup (8),
.BR netstat (1),
.BR scutil (8)
